  "answer": "### Issue Presented\n\nHowever, since the gross receipts are below the threshold, the designer is not mandated to register for VAT. If the designer anticipates that their gross receipts will exceed ₱3 million in the next 12 months, they should register for VAT as per Section 236 of the NIRC, which outlines the registration requirements for VAT. \n\nIn summary, based on the current gross receipts, VAT registration is not required unless future projections indicate exceeding the threshold.\n\n### Relevant Facts / Assumptions\nThe factual circumstances have not been fully described. The analysis is based on the question as presented.\n\n### Alternative Interpretations\nNo alternative interpretations identified from the available indexed authorities.\n\n### Position Strength\nPosition strength is preliminary and subject to full fact pattern verification.",
